Separate processes (not linked, not distributed as part of this binary)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

get-product-name 1.19.0 — used by the optional extraction sidecar
  https://github.com/Wingysam/get-product-data  (npm package: get-product-name)
  MIT — Copyright 2020 Sam Wing. Verified against the package metadata and the
  repository LICENSE file.

  Note the naming: the npm package is "get-product-name" while the repository
  it is published from is named "get-product-data". They are the same library.

  It runs as a separate process invoked over HTTP, is not linked into this
  binary, and is not redistributed as part of it. The parent project it was
  written for (Christmas Community) is AGPL-3.0, but the library itself is not,
  so no copyleft obligation attaches to this Apache-2.0 codebase either way.

  The sidecar is optional. With EXTRACTOR_SIDECAR_URL unset, no part of it is
  used, built, or shipped.

